# Rust practices (Spec Chum)

Follow [Rust API Guidelines](https://rust-lang.github.io/api-guidelines/) when designing public crate APIs.

## Errors

```rust
// ✅ library crates
#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
pub enum LoadError {
    #[error("invalid header")]
    BadHeader,
    #[error(transparent)]
    Io(#[from] std::io::Error),
}

// ✅ app / binaries
fn run() -> anyhow::Result<()> { /* ... */ Ok(()) }

// ❌ non-test library / hot paths
let v = x.unwrap();
```

## Safety & style

- `unsafe_code` is denied via workspace lints. Prefer safe APIs; if `unsafe` is unavoidable, isolate it and document `// SAFETY: ...`.
- Prefer `&T` / iterators over needless clones; avoid `clone()` in T-state hot loops (Z80/ULA).
- Derive `Debug` on public types; keep APIs small (`pub(crate)` by default).
- Use `?` for propagation; no empty `catch` / discarded `Result`s.

## Verification

```bash
./scripts/check.sh
```

Fix fmt/clippy/test failures before considering the change complete.
